Z||000000||mshill||12-23-1999||02:21 PM||||I had an exhaust leak (86SE V6) that was a tick-tick at idle but a very distinguisable put-put (like a Volkswagen bug makes) on acceleration.<P>This morning when I went to leave the house the put-put sound was gone and replaced by a puff-puff (like there was no compression or detonation) and the power seemed to be way down.<P>I think I just lost a cylinder.  I will find out this afternoon when I am able to do a compression test.||||reg||5
Z||000001||CUTTER||12-23-1999||11:21 PM||||Sounds like a CAT. to me Thats what mine did when it was going.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||12-24-1999||01:21 AM||||Cutter, my cat is brand new, less than 1000 miles. <P>I checked the compression and it is good on all six cylinders and I have srong spark as well.  I need to get my timing light to working to see if my timing chain jumped.  It runs as if the timing was retarded (very smooth but no power).<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000003||Phil||12-24-1999||07:22 AM||||Are your exhaust manifolds cracked or broken?||||reg||1
Z||000004||mshill||12-24-1999||03:27 PM||||Phil,  I am not sure where the exhaust leak is but is is possible it is at the manifold. <P>Another update.  Timing is good.  When I put the ECM in diagnostic mode, the exhaust leak comes back as it was before.  TPS and MAP sensor are good also (swapped with my GT). And the O2 sensor is 1 month old.<P>It idles smooth, but when you give it gas it is obviously lacking power, and if I really put my foot down it really stumbles bad.<P>Something I just now checked was that there seems to be little or no exhaust coming out of the tail pipes.  I am leaning towards a clogged cat or muffler.  What in the world would cause a cat to clog in less than 1000 miles?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 12-24-1999).]||||reg||1
